sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: stage 1 of the command development pipeline. Prepare the chart, page and cases as the first commit on the feature branch. Build and prove the feature in stages 2 and 3 before stage 4 opens its one PR. This is the contributor workflow, not an automated prep operation.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: development pipeline stage 1 · spec first, before code or PR
  %% kind: pipeline.1-prep
  autonumber
  %% lane AG icon=terminal pill=author tone=gray
  %% lane CP icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  %% lane RV icon=terminal pill=reviewer tone=amber
  participant AG as Author<br/>agent or person
  participant CP as Task copy<br/>feature branch
  participant RV as Reviewer<br/>independent agent
  AG->>CP: Read the owning contracts<br/>brief · chart · page · code
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - settle the supported inputs, outcomes, refusals, repeat behavior and failure recovery from the brief and current decisions
  %%> - read code to identify the gap, not to narrow the agreed behavior
  AG->>CP: Draft the chart<br/>flow-tighten · chart rules
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - follows docs/cli/README.md and the flow-tighten skill; the chart states the intended flow before implementation
  %%> - shows meaningful alternate outcomes and what remains after failure
  AG->>CP: Write the page<br/>usage · behavior · errors
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - follows the chart and links shared rules instead of repeating them
  AG->>CP: Design the proof cases<br/>chart paths · batches
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - derives cases from the chart and page; checks real effects, repeats, refusals and recovery where applicable
  %%> - keeps existing runnable cases unless their behavior is removed; records runner gaps under uncovered instead of inventing steps
  %%> - fails_today records a runnable case that current code fails; fails_on_base metadata does not cause replay in copy proofs
  AG->>CP: Check the spec<br/>flows · docs · runner plan
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - bin/check-flows, composer docs-build and composer docs-lint pass
  %%> - the runner plan accepts the cases file, and the runner tests pass; a plan is not execution proof
  AG->>RV: Review the spec<br/>chart · page · cases
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - a fresh read-only reviewer checks the intended behavior and case coverage against their owning rules
  loop findings remain
    RV-->>AG: Findings<br/>file · reason
    AG->>CP: Correct the spec<br/>repeat checks and review
    %%> Result:
    %%> - unresolved product choices go to the owner before implementation
  end
  AG->>CP: Commit the spec first<br/>chart · page · cases only
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the first commit on the feature branch holds the spec, with no implementation code
  %%> - a changed chart stays draft until the owner approves it; authoring or a clean agent review does not mark it reviewed
  Note over AG,CP: Build, then prove<br/>no PR opens yet
  %%> Result:
  %%> - stages 2 and 3 build and prove the feature end to end in this task copy and its nested fleet before any PR, draft or ready, opens
